From 17a44c1b9ddfb1ff0e9f9372c29f106918d70e0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chun-Yi Lee <jlee@suse.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:48:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] shim: Allow overriding FALLBACK and MOK_MANAGER filenames at
 compile time

Currently, the fallback and MokManager binary paths in shim are
hardcoded to "fb<EFI_ARCH>.efi" and "mm<EFI_ARCH>.efi" via the
FALLBACK and MOK_MANAGER macros.

Downstream distributions or specific bootloader setups may rename or
install these binaries under different filenames (for instance,
standardized names like "fallback.efi" and "MokManager.efi", or
names tailored to distribution-specific filesystem layouts). Because
these macros are unconditionally defined in the source header/file,
build environments cannot adjust the target binaries at build time
without patching the source tree.

Guard the definitions of FALLBACK and MOK_MANAGER with #ifndef checks.
Fall back to the upstream default filenames when these macros are not
defined externally. This allows downstream build systems to override the
target binary filenames at compile time (e.g., via EXTRA_DEFINES) while
preserving existing default behavior.

This patch is sent to upstream for reviewing.

Link: https://github.com/rhboot/shim/pull/837
Signed-off-by: Chun-Yi Lee <jlee@suse.com>
---
 shim.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

Index: shim-16.1/shim.h
===================================================================
--- shim-16.1.orig/shim.h
+++ shim-16.1/shim.h
@@ -133,8 +133,12 @@
 #define DEBUGSRC L"/usr/src/debug/shim-" VERSIONSTR "." EFI_ARCH
 #endif
 
+#ifndef FALLBACK
 #define FALLBACK L"\\fb" EFI_ARCH L".efi"
+#endif
+#ifndef MOK_MANAGER
 #define MOK_MANAGER L"\\mm" EFI_ARCH L".efi"
+#endif
 
 #if defined(VENDOR_DB_FILE)
 # define vendor_authorized vendor_db
